id: pm-iktj
title: "Uniform stdin convention: body-file and annotation --file flags accept '-' for stdin"
description: "Standardize stdin handling so every file-valued flag that accepts external content can use '-' for stdin, giving scripts and agents one predictable convention for generated bodies, reasons, and documents."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[3]: agent-ux,"area:cli",composability
created_at: "2026-07-06T22:10:15.407Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-24T08:44:26.007Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-24T08:41:53.424Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-24T08:41:53.424Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: All file-reading flags across commands accept '-' to read stdin (inventory taken from contracts); behavior documented in the scripting contract (pm-psy1); error message for unreadable paths mentions the '-' option; tests cover piped heredoc usage; no behavior change for real paths
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "File, CLI stdin, SDK stdin-token, and MCP document sources remain unambiguous before any stream read."
actual_result: "Bulk body/ID inputs compose across CLI, SDK, MCP, and atomic structured transactions without fail-open selectors or competing stdin reads. MCP mutation payloads treat dash sentinels as literal data, refuse server-local annotation file reads, and preserve direct CLI/SDK file/stdin semantics; full exact coverage and repository assurance pass."
