  pm-fs8q9x,implements,"2026-07-26T05:59:31.644Z"
comments[19]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-23T20:29:26.533Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-23: contract-derived census and shared SDK file-or-stdin primitive will cover every external-content --*-file surface, preserve real-path behavior, improve unreadable-path recovery, and prove piped heredoc use. Canonical pm-iktj is reused after all-status duplicate verification."
  "2026-08-23T21:57:50.433Z","harness:codex","Tracker repair evidence: removed only the newly added duplicate pm-m9xv implements row by its exact created_at signature; the canonical 2026-07-25 relationship remains intact."
  "2026-08-23T22:05:18.542Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence 2026-08-24: every external-content file flag in this scope accepts '-' as stdin through the shared SDK token resolver: update/close --body-file plus comments, notes, and learnings --file. Real paths retain prior behavior and unreadable/missing input produces structured recovery. CLI invocation contracts now declare argv/file/stdin modes and the docs include heredoc/pipeline examples. Focused linked tests, the disposable-tracker body-stdin check, 7,858-test exact 100% coverage, typecheck, security scan, and the complete lint/static stack pass. The duplicate relationship added during reconciliation was removed by exact signature; the canonical historical implements edge remains."
  "2026-08-23T22:39:08.695Z","harness:codex","Review finding: --body-file - creates an isolated stdin resolver after --description - or --stdin-json can consume the stream, causing unsettled-await exit/hang. Add an up-front command-wide single-consumer refusal and real-process regression proof."
  "2026-08-23T22:48:45.194Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence 2026-08-24: command-wide stdin ownership is validated before --stdin-json, --description -, --body-file -, or bulk --ids - can read. Competing consumers fail with usage exit 2 rather than an unsettled second read; real-process negative controls and registration/contract unit tests pass. All three linked-test groups pass in isolated schema trackers with local_source_ref trust and zero trust, assertion, or infrastructure failures. Final full proof passes 570 files / 7,858 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-08-23T22:59:19.204Z","harness:codex","Security re-review finding: resolveBodyFileContent trims its path before recognizing '-', but the command preflight compared the raw value. --description - with --body-file ' - ' could still reach a second read. Normalize the preflight and prove whitespace-token refusal in a real process."
  "2026-08-23T23:07:40.344Z","harness:codex","Bugbot re-review finding: the generated changelog inherited the item's illustrative close --reason-file wording even though no such option exists. Narrow the canonical title to the implemented body-file and annotation --file surfaces, then regenerate package-owned release notes."
  "2026-08-23T23:08:03.430Z","harness:codex","Second review-fix evidence 2026-08-24: --description - plus --body-file ' - ' now refuses before any read with exit 2, closing the whitespace normalization bypass. The canonical title and generated release note are narrowed to implemented body-file and annotation --file surfaces. Linked tests and the full 7,858-test exact-coverage run pass."
  "2026-08-24T02:31:55.669Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence: --body-file invocation metadata now documents both file input and '-' stdin input; repeated competing-stdin regressions share one helper without weakening coverage. Linked file/stdin suites passed 101/101 across three commands; full exact coverage passed 570 files / 7870 tests at 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines. Contract snapshot, typecheck, ESLint, duplicate scan, repository static-quality gates, and secret scan passed."
  "2026-08-24T04:00:19.910Z","harness:codex","Exact-head recurrence fix evidence 2026-08-24: create/update mark only the body resolved from --body-file as literal transport data, so content equal to '-' is stored verbatim while a separate explicit flag such as --comment - can still consume stdin. Real-process regressions cover create from --body-file - with exact-dash stdin, update from a real file containing only '-', and simultaneous comment stdin. All four linked tests passed with local_source_ref trust and zero failure categories. Final exact coverage passed 570 files / 7,873 tests at 100/100/100/100; public SDK snapshot is additive/current and the full zero-duplicate static-quality stack passes."
  "2026-08-24T04:02:30.899Z","harness:codex","Closeout evidence: regenerated package-owned CHANGELOG.md from all release-tag windows with public .agents/pm links after final recurrence closure; deterministic --check is unchanged at 2,186 items and 393,190 bytes. ESLint, zero-clone scan, credential scan, and pnpm audit (no known vulnerabilities) pass."
  "2026-08-24T04:08:19.448Z","harness:codex","Correction: the repository-owned changelog gate installs pm-changelog and generates with --exclude-tag changelog-exclude. The exact deterministic result is 2,181 items and 392,254 bytes; the earlier 2,186-item / 393,190-byte comment included five intentionally excluded historical entries and is superseded by this evidence."
  "2026-08-24T04:09:14.545Z","harness:codex","Exact-head security review finding: transport-decoded MCP body/annotation values must remain literal, and direct SDK competing stdin tokens must be rejected before any stream read. Extend the shared stdin policy and add MCP plus open-stream refusal regressions."
  "2026-08-24T04:46:05.456Z","harness:codex","Final exact-head evidence: transport provenance now flows through the existing SDK input normalizer, so MCP dash documents never consume JSON-RPC stdin; direct SDK conflicts preflight the complete mutation field plan before any stream read. Create/update/update-many/append regressions pass, all five linked tests are trusted and green, full static assurance passes, and exact 570-file / 7,877-test coverage is 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-24T04:55:13.954Z","harness:codex","Exact-head security review at 53333b5389d62ae928815585049eae26d3658ec0 found two remaining MCP stdin transport boundaries: Plan-derived create options lose the literal marker, and annotation adapters can consume JSON-RPC stdin for dash/stdin inputs. Reopened only this actively edited item; pm-3oq022 remains closed/released because bulk selector semantics and update-many transport are clear."
  "2026-08-24T05:56:30.948Z","harness:codex","Final review-fix evidence 2026-08-24: MCP literal provenance now survives Plan-derived create options, meet/event/remind adapters, and comments/notes/learnings normalization. Dash document values remain literal; annotation stdin:true and file:'-' fail closed with structured mcp_stdin_unavailable recovery without reading JSON-RPC stdin. A spawned full-profile MCP process with stdin intentionally left open returns the Plan response, closing the prior hang. All 6 linked commands passed with local_source_ref trust and zero failure categories. Full verification passed 570/570 files and 7,879/7,879 tests with exact 100% statements (57,542), branches (43,063), functions (11,974), and lines (55,462); the complete static suite exited 0 after package/API, 2,838-flag, 117-refusal, tracker, graph, and record-integrity gates."
  "2026-08-24T08:07:58.840Z","harness:codex","Exact-head security review at 50d1735b049ef6140cd2543f9cf2249c4115cc2b found a high-severity MCP boundary gap: annotation options.file accepted arbitrary server-local paths despite schema warnings. Reopened only this item to reject MCP annotation file sources at runtime while preserving CLI/direct SDK file behavior, with a real-process /etc/hostname negative regression."
  "2026-08-24T08:41:43.103Z","harness:codex","Evidence: closed the exact-head review findings by refusing comments/notes/learnings file input at the MCP boundary with mcp_annotation_file_unavailable while preserving CLI/direct SDK file support; a real MCP process with stdin kept open refused /etc/hostname, stored no annotation, and served a later Plan request. Atomic CLI JSON and MCP pm_mutate transactions now preserve structured description/body '-' values literally through parser, transaction overlays, and runtime option cloning, so the two-row transaction commits without a second stdin read or partial write. Verification: focused 69/69; full exact coverage 570 files and 7,880 tests at 100% statements (57,553/57,553), branches (43,079/43,079), functions (11,978/11,978), lines (55,474/55,474); pnpm typecheck passed; CI=1 pnpm quality:static passed all repository, refusal, package, SDK, graph, and record gates; 7/7 linked tests passed with local_source_ref trust and infra_collision=0, trust_refusal=0, assertion_failure=0, empty_run=0, timeout=0, max_buffer=0, spawn_error=0, signal=0."
  "2026-08-24T08:44:26.007Z","harness:codex","Closeout diagnostics: deterministic changelog generation/check remained unchanged at 2,181 items and 392,254 bytes; pm validate passed with history drift 0 and only the unchanged 295 legacy resolution warnings; pm health --check-only passed all 10 checks with 14 legacy hierarchy advisories. Item is closed and claim released."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-15T19:27:03.514Z",maintainer-agent,"Dogfood confirmation 2026-07-15 (review pass #89): pm create --body-file - fails ENOENT body_file_unreadable (tries to open a file literally named \"-\"), forcing a scratch-file workaround mid-review. The error's own next_steps suggest \"ls -l \\\"-\\\"\" — the recovery bundle does not know stdin is the intent. This is exactly the convention gap this item owns; --body-file should be first on the flag list when implementing."
